        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "9a4e1152-2ae3-5651-92cd-e3c73adef551",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Paul Cook, Matthew Ashman, Lance Burman\n- Bands: Sex Pistols, Chiefs of Relief, Agent Provocateur\n- Places: Hammersmith, London\n- Roles: drummer, guitarist, vocalist\n- Topics: punk rock, electro-punk\n\nFacts:\n- The Sex Pistols were an English punk rock band formed in London in 1975.\n- Paul Thomas Cook was born on 20 July 1956 in Hammersmith, London.\n- Paul Cook is an English drummer and a member of the Sex Pistols.\n- Chiefs of Relief were a British rock group with an electro-punk style.\n- Matthew Ashman was the vocalist and guitarist of Chiefs of Relief.\n- Paul Cook was also a drummer in Chiefs of Relief.\n- When Matthew Ashman died in 1995, Lance Burman, formerly of Chiefs of Relief, replaced him on guitar in Agent Provocateur.",
